 Psalms is equivalent to the English word “instruction,” or to become wise by instruction; hence, : “Sing ye praises with understanding.”)","r":["19.47.7"]},{"d":1,"t":"MICAHTAM"},{"d":2,"t":"A musical term in the titles of","r":["19.16.1","19.56.1","19.57.1","19.58.1","19.59.1","19.60.1"]},{"d":2,"t":"(Luther interprets this as “golden,” that is, “precious.” Ewald interprets it as signifying a plaintive manner.)"},{"d":1,"t":"MUTH-LABBEN"},{"d":2,"t":"In the title of","r":["19.9.1"]},{"d":2,"t":"(Authorities, ancient and modern, differ as to the probable signification. Gesenius and De Wette interpret it, “with the voice of virgins, by boys.” Others derive the word from a different Hebrew root, and interpret it as indicating that the Psalm was a funeral ode.)"},{"d":1,"t":"NEGINAH and NEGINOTH"},{"d":2,"t":"Appear in the titles of","r":["19.4.1","19.54.1","19.55.1","19.61.1","19.67.1","35.3.19"]},{"d":2,"t":"(Its use seems to have been to indicate that the song should be accompanied by stringed instruments.) -NEHILOTH"},{"d":2,"t":"Appears in the title of","r":["19.5.1"]},{"d":2,"t":"(It seems to indicate, according to Gesenius, that when this Psalm was sung it was to be accompanied by wind instruments.) -SELAH"},{"d":2,"t":"(This term appears frequently in the Psalms. Its use is not known. Possibly it signified a pause in the vocal music while an instrumental interlude or finale was rendered.)"},{"d":1,"t":"SHEMINITH"},{"d":2,"t":"In the titles of","r":["19.6.1","19.12.1"]},{"d":2,"t":"(Translated “eighth,” probably indicates the measure, movement, or pitch.)"},{"d":1,"t":"SHIGGAION"},{"d":2,"t":"In the title of","r":["19.7.1"]},{"d":2,"t":"And its plural, SHIGIONOTH, in the title of","r":["35.3.1"]},{"d":2,"t":"(Supposed to be a musical term to guide in rendering the song. At the close of the chapter, the author refers the ode “to the chief musician, on my stringed instruments.” The term may suggest the movement in interpreting the music set to it.)"},{"d":1,"t":"SHOSHANNIM and SHUSHAN-EDUTH.In the titles to","r":["19.45.1","19.60.1","19.69.1","19.80.1"]},{"d":2,"t":"(Seems to indicate the manner in which these Psalms were to be rendered. Kimchi, Tremellius, and Eichhorn render it “hexachorda,” that is, that in singing these Psalms instruments of six strings were to accompany.)"},{"d":1,"t":"UNCLASSIFIED SCRIPTURES RELATING TO","r":["1.31.27","2.15.1","2.15.20","2.15.21","2.21.17-20","7.5.1-3","7.11.34","9.18.6","9.18.7","10.19.35","11.1.40","13.6.31","13.6.32","13.15.16-22","13.15.24","13.15.27","13.15.28","13.16.4-39","13.16.41","13.16.42","13.22.3","13.22.5","13.22.6","13.25.1","13.25.5","13.25.6","13.25.7","13.25.8","14.5.12","14.5.13","14.20.19","14.20.21","14.20.22","14.20.28","14.23.13","14.23.18","14.29.25-28","14.31.2","14.35.15","14.35.25","15.2.64","15.3.10","15.3.11","16.12.24","16.12.27-31","18.21.12","18.30.31","19.33.1-4","19.68.4","19.68.25","19.68.26","19.68.32-35","19.81.1-3","19.87.7","19.92.1-3","19.95.1","19.95.2","19.98.1-8","19.104.33","19.105.2","19.135.1","19.135.2","19.135.3","19.137.1-6","19.144.9","19.149.1-3","19.149.6","19.150.1-6","20.25.20","21.2.8","23.5.12","23.14.11","23.16.10","23.23.16","23.24.8","23.24.9","23.30.29","23.30.32","24.31.4","26.26.13","26.33.32","27.3.4","27.3.6","27.3.7","30.6.5","30.8.10","40.9.23","40.11.17","41.14.26","46.14.15","49.5.19","51.3.16","58.2.12","66.14.2","66.14.3","66.18.22"]},{"d":1,"t":"See","s":[["PRAISE",3933]]},{"d":1,"t":"See","s":[["PSALMS",3986]]}]},"3466":{"h":"MUSTARD","l":[{"d":1,"t":"General scriptures concerning","r":["40.13.31","40.13.32"]}]},"3467":{"h":"MUSTER","l":[{"d":1,"t":"Of troops","r":["9.14.17","10.20.4","11.20.26","12.25.19","23.13.4"]},{"d":1,"t":"See","s":[["ARMIES",390]]}]},"3468":{"h":"MUTH-LABBEN","l":[{"d":1,"t":"See","s":[["MUSIC",3465]]}]},"3469":{"h":"MUTINY","l":[{"d":1,"t":"Israelites against Moses","r":["4.14.4"]},{"d":1,"t":"See","s":[["CONSPIRACY",1203]]}]},"3470":{"h":"MYRA","l":[{"d":1,"t":"A city of Lycia; Paul vis